[
  {
    "sha": "6885456aa178e0dff2fca3faa5c3378392cab49e",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDY4ODU0NTZhYTE3OGUwZGZmMmZjYTNmYWE1YzMzNzgzOTJjYWI0OWU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-23T05:08:40Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-23T05:08:40Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): the plain 3D finish hop never goes below the run end\n\nThe plain hop of emit_runs took its travel plane from the retract\nplane and the next run start only. With a retract plane below the end\nof the current run (a cavity with Contour, or a convex part cut inner\nfirst), the tool fed down into the part at the run end and made a\nrapid through it. The verifier held the post (envelope gouge 3 mm,\nrapid in stock), so nothing passed silently.\n\nThe hop plane is now never below the run end. The move across is made\nat that plane only if the plane is over every facet or the exact sweep\n(gaplink::straight_ok) clears it; else the hop goes to clearance. With\na retract plane at or above the model top the hop is unchanged.\n\nFixes #3627\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
